Andrew Janedy Comp426_001 Project2

This project fulfills the requirements of:

* A window no smaller than 500 x 500 pixels and no greater than 1500 x 1500 pixels
* A tiled map that is 15 x 15 tiles
* A barrier type tile
* Two NPC sprites that move at random and animate on contact with the player sprite
* An animated player sprite that has "different" animations for up down left and right
    * The player sprite cannot move through barrier tiles (unless you find THE bug)
    * The player sprite cannot pass through the NPC sprites (in fact the hitbox is pretty big so don't go near them)

Additional attributes that were not required in the project specifications:

* There are additional sprites that the player sprite can consume
* Consuming bread sprites adds to a score counter
* High score is monitored and displayed as well as the game score, game reads and writes from and to a high score file
* There are also a small collection of game sounds


All requirements of this project have been met

Barrier is easily recognizable as there are only two tiles and you start the game moving through one

NPC sprites are the big scary alligators.  Do not go near them, they can lunge kinda far

Game tiles, alligator sprites, and player sprite were drawn, from scratch, by me, using MSPaint.


